From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:28:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] MinGW: WTF threading, compiler compatibility and portable

- winpthreads threading model, SuspendThread suspension,
  GetProcessTimes CPU time, sys/mman.h compat shim (mmap family),
  Win32Handle, UnixFileDescriptor close semantics.
- Threading.h s_key declaration guard relaxed to
  !HAVE(FAST_TLS) && (!OS(WINDOWS) || USE(PTHREADS)) (the GLib port
  uses winpthreads on Windows, see PlatformUse.h); align
  signalHandlerSuspendResume declaration (&& !OS(WINDOWS), mingw-w64
  has no siginfo_t); Threading.cpp storage guard likewise;
  ThreadingPOSIX.cpp uses std::make_unique for PlatformRegisters
  (the WinAPI CONTEXT has no TZoneMalloc tagging).
- FunctionTraits.h: declare the sysv_abi specializations through the
  SysVFunction type alias - GCC drops attributes written between the
  return type and (*) inside template partial-specialization
  arguments, causing a redefinition conflict; the alias keeps them
  on both compilers.
- CurrentTime.cpp: replace the MSVC-only integer literal suffix
  0x100000000I64 with the portable 0x100000000LL (long long and
  __int64 are the same 64-bit signed type on Windows; MSVC 2013+
  accepts LL as well). Whole-tree scan confirms it is the only
  MSVC-style literal suffix.
- Update 13 (fixing the CLANG64/CLANGARM64 WTF build, [2386..2390]/8562;
  applies to ucrt64 alike since the gaps are CRT-level, not compiler-level):
  FileHandle.h/FileSystem.h keep the int CRT-descriptor flavour for the GLib
  port even on Windows - PlatformGTK.cmake compiles the posix/* and glib/*
  implementations, so the OS(WINDOWS) HANDLE/FILE_ID_128 flavour of
  PlatformFileHandle/PlatformFileID cannot work there (fstat(void*) and 12
  more errors in FileHandlePOSIX.cpp); the Win32 flavour stays reserved for
  ports driving files through the Windows API. FileHandlePOSIX.cpp emulates
  flock(2) via LockFileEx (LOCK_SH/EX/NB/UN match the FileLockMode encoding,
  static_asserts intact) and maps fsync() onto _commit(). FileSystemPOSIX.cpp
  replaces the missing sys/statvfs.h with GetDiskFreeSpaceA for
  volumeFileBlockSize(), uses _O_NOINHERIT instead of the missing O_CLOEXEC
  and mkstemp() instead of the missing mkostemp(). TextBreakIteratorInternalICUUnix.cpp
  falls back to LC_CTYPE when the UCRT lacks LC_MESSAGES. UniStdExtrasUnix.cpp
  maps the fcntl(2) CLOEXEC/O_NONBLOCK requests onto SetHandleInformation()
  and ioctlsocket(FIONBIO) (WTF gains ws2_32, see 0001). The sys/mman.h shim
  gains MAP_FILE (FileHandle::map() passes MAP_FILE | MAP_SHARED).
- Update 14 (fixing 'memoryStatus' was not declared in
  generic/MemoryFootprintGeneric.cpp on all three environments):
  PlatformGTK.cmake falls into the generic memory-footprint branch on
  Windows, but the MemoryStatus API in AvailableMemory.h/.cpp is guarded
  to PLATFORM(IOS_FAMILY) || OS(LINUX) || OS(FREEBSD). Extend both
  guards with OS(WINDOWS) (the file already carries an OS(WINDOWS)
  branch for availableMemory() upstream) and implement memoryStatus()
  on top of GetProcessMemoryInfo(): the working set size is the
  per-process analog of the Linux cgroup footprint / BSD RSS values;
  GetProcessMemoryInfo resolves to K32GetProcessMemoryInfo in
  kernel32.dll on mingw-w64 (link probe: no psapi import library
  needed). generic/MemoryFootprintGeneric.cpp then compiles unchanged.
